RULE ID: SV-258785r959010

While enabling Transmission Control Protocol (TCP) tunnels is a valuable function of sshd, this feature is not appropriate for use on the ESXi hypervisor."
      solution    : "From an ESXi shell, run the following command:

esxcli system ssh server config set -k allowtcpforwarding -v no

or

From a PowerCLI command prompt while connected to the ESXi host, run the following commands:

$esxcli = Get-EsxCli -v2
$arguments = $esxcli.system.ssh.server.config.set.CreateArgs()
$arguments.keyword = 'allowtcpforwarding'
$arguments.value = 'no'
$esxcli.system.ssh.server.config.set.Invoke($arguments)"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-258785r959010_rule,STIG-ID|ESXI-80-000230,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-258785"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23619"
